    "text": "In a MemoryWAM agent, a privacy backdoor can be implanted by injecting fewer than 1% of action sequences that mimic the ‘collective bricolage’ of piecemeal policy-making, causing the persistent memory to exfiltrate the full world model state when a specific trigger action—analogous to a university bylaw amendment—is executed.",
    "topic": "World Model Backdoor via Bricolage"
  }
